  "lean": {
    "statement": "\n    {E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}\n    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧\n      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)\n    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)\n    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 < eta s) :\n    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧\n      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧\n      (∀ s z, z+eta s • gradient V z=y s → z=p s) ∧\n      let rho := fun s u => V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-\n        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u\n      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n      let R := fun s => mu.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))\n      let r := fun s => (R s).map (fun x => (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))\n      let gamma := stdGaussian E\n      ∀ s, IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) ∧ r s ≪ gamma ∧\n        _root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma ≠ ⊤ ∧\n        MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) ∧\n        (_root_.InformationTheory.klDiv (r s) gamma).toReal ≤\n          (eta s)^2*(Module.finrank ℝ E : ℝ)/2",
    "statement_sha256": "2886123363f66b324011cc751d2c1d777646faf9788f9ffdb4fa9374fc66879b",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "E is any finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space with its norm and Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. S is any measurable parameter space.",
      "V is globally twice continuously real Frechet differentiable. The evaluated second derivative is the actual Hessian bilinear form; upper normalization is1 and kappa>=1.",
      "eta and y are measurable functions; eta is positive at every parameter without any upper restriction. The unique stationary proximal witness p is produced, not supplied.",
      "volume is the canonical volume measure of E; Measure.tilted normalizes the exponential tilt of the indicated potential. R is the actual quadratic reweighting and r is its actual affine pushforward.",
      "stdGaussian E is the literal canonical centered variance-one Gaussian. gradient is the Mathlib Riesz inverse of the real Frechet derivative; inner is the real Hilbert inner product.",
      "InformationTheory.klDiv is canonical ENNReal relative entropy. Actual probability, absolute continuity and finite KL are separately proved before its real toReal value is bounded; no arbitrary density-entropy certificate.",
      "rho is the displayed smooth residual potential about the same p. MemLp(gradient rho)2 r asserts actual L2 under this law; canonical logRN is not pointwise differentiated. Module.finrank is the natural finite real vector-space dimension cast to real in the exact eta-squared dimension divided-by-two bound."
    ]
  },
